  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThe greatest heat impacts are now occurring across the FA this \nafternoon as a cold front begins to approach the FA from the \nnorthwest. A deep 500 mb trough is also digging into the Ohio Valley \nand will bring a significantly cooler airmass for the second half of \nthe week with temperatures falling 10 degrees below normal. Highs \nwill range from the upper 70s to lower 80s Wednesday through Friday. \nIn the meantime, there is the potential for a few severe storms this \nafternoon and evening as the aformentioned front sweeps through. \n\nThe front quad of a 50 kt jet max at 500 mb is now approaching with \nSBCAPE values in the 5500 to 6500 J/kg range. The best effective \nbulk shear is setting up along our eastern counties with a gradient \nof 20-40 kts. Combined with a 30-35K theta-e difference and DCAPE \nvalues around 800-1000 J/kg, the potential for strong damaging wind \ngusts of 60-70 mph remains the main hazard of concern. Isolated \nlarge hail near 1 inch is also possible, but the extremely warm \nboundary layer may simply mean a lot of melting. While the low-level \nshear is not the greatest, there is a non-zero chance of a isolated\ntornado, especially over southwest Indiana. Torrential downpours\nwill also be capable of causing runoff on roadways as there is \nample moisture in the column with sfc mixing ratios around 20-22\ng/kg and 2.2-2.3\" peak PWATs. \n\nSfc high pressure currently over Saskatchewan will provide a break \nfrom the active weather pattern Wednesday through Thursday before \nrain chances begin to return on Friday as a shortwave ejects over \nthe central Plains. The eastern extent of a ridge of high pressure \nbegins to build in over the weekend, with high temperatures climbing \nback into the 90s by Sunday along with an increase in humidity. ML \nguidance is hinting at the potential for additional severe weather \nbetween Sunday and next Tuesday, as multiple disturbances ride along \nthe ridge. Rain chances will be intermittent during this period.",
